</section>
<section id="A3.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.5 </span>Comparison between Single-dataset and Multi-dataset Training</h3>

<div id="A3.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We also compare the performance of ZO Fine-tuner under single-dataset and multi-dataset training settings. In the multi-dataset setting, we construct a diverse training set by selecting one representative dataset from each task type: SST-2 for sentiment analysis, CB and COPA for natural language inference, and SQuAD for question answering. For the single-dataset setting, the optimizer is trained solely on COPA.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS5.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS5.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The multi-dataset setting could lead to better performance. However, as shown in Figure <a href="#A3.F6" title="Figure 6 ‣ C.5 Comparison between Single-dataset and Multi-dataset Training ‣ Appendix C Additional Experimental Results ‣ Learning a Zeroth-Order Optimizer for Fine-Tuning LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>, in some cases, the ZO Fine-tuner trained on a single dataset can outperform its multi-dataset counterpart. Overall, the two settings yield comparable performance. Single-dataset training is also simpler to implement and tune, while still achieving competitive results. And that’s why we choose to use it throughout the main experiments.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A3.F6" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A3.F6.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2510.00419v1/figures/llama1b_cb_single_vs_multi.png" id="A3.F6.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:548/327;" width="548" height="327" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(a) </span>CB + LLaMA-1B</figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A3.F6.sf2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2510.00419v1/figures/llama8b_drop_single_vs_multi.png" id="A3.F6.sf2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:548/327;" width="548" height="327" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(b) </span>DROP + LLaMA-8B</figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 6: </span>
Comparison of inference loss between ZO Fine-tuners trained with single-dataset and multi-dataset settings. Results are reported on CB task using LLaMA-1B (left) and on DROP task LLaMA-8B (right). The single-dataset variant is trained solely on COPA, while the multi-dataset variant is jointly trained on COPA, SST-2, and SQuAD.
</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Theoretical Analysis</h2>

<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we formally discuss our theoretical results and derive theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1 (Informal Version). ‣ 3.1 Motivation ‣ 3 Method ‣ Learning a Zeroth-Order Optimizer for Fine-Tuning LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>. First, we set up the notations and definition we need and formally present the theorem.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmdefinition1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmdefinition1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 1</span></span><span id="Thmdefinition1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Expected Loss Change)<span id="Thmdefinition1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmdefinition1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmdefinition1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmdefinition1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The expected change in loss after performing a one-step update from parameter <math id="Thmdefinition1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is defined as</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d(\theta_{t}):=\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{L}(\theta_{t+1})\mid\theta_{t}]-\mathcal{L}(\theta_{t})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d(\theta_{t}):=\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{L}(\theta_{t+1})\mid\theta_{t}]-\mathcal{L}(\theta_{t}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmassumption1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_assumption">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmassumption1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Assumption 1</span></span><span id="Thmassumption1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Local <math id="Thmassumption1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>-effective rank)<span id="Thmassumption1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmassumption1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmassumption1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmassumption1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmassumption1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G(\theta_{t})=\max_{(x,y)\in D}\|\nabla\mathcal{L}(\theta_{t};\{(x,y)\})\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G(\theta_{t})=\max_{(x,y)\in D}\|\nabla\mathcal{L}(\theta_{t};\{(x,y)\})\|</annotation></semantics></math>. There exists a matrix <math id="Thmassumption1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(\theta_{t})\leq\ell\cdot I_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(\theta_{t})\leq\ell\cdot I_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> such that:</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<ol id="A4.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A4.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For all <math id="A4.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A4.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\theta-\theta_{t}\|\leq\eta dG(\theta_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\theta-\theta_{t}\|\leq\eta dG(\theta_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A4.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla^{2}\mathcal{L}(\theta)\preceq H(\theta_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mo>∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla^{2}\mathcal{L}(\theta)\preceq H(\theta_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The effective rank of <math id="A4.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(\theta_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(\theta_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e. <math id="A4.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{tr}(H(\theta_{t}))/\|H(\theta_{t})\|_{\mathrm{op}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{tr}(H(\theta_{t}))/\|H(\theta_{t})\|_{\mathrm{op}}</annotation></semantics></math>, is at most <math id="A4.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 2</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under Assumption 1, the expected loss change after one-step update of MeZO has upper bound as follows, where <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{MB}=\mathrm{Cov}(\nabla\mathcal{L}(\theta_{t};\{(x_{i},y_{i})\}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{MB}=\mathrm{Cov}(\nabla\mathcal{L}(\theta_{t};\{(x_{i},y_{i})\}))</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle d_{\mathrm{MeZO}}(\theta_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>MeZO</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle d_{\mathrm{MeZO}}(\theta_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{L}(\theta_{t+1})|\theta_{t}]-\mathcal{L}(\theta_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{L}(\theta_{t+1})|\theta_{t}]-\mathcal{L}(\theta_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq-\eta\|\nabla\mathcal{L}(\theta_{t})\|^{2}+\frac{\eta^{2}\ell}{2}\cdot\left(\frac{dr+d-2}{d+2}+1\right)\cdot\left(\|\nabla\mathcal{L}(\theta_{t})\|^{2}+\frac{1}{B}\mathrm{tr}(\Sigma_{MB}(\theta_{t}))\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>B</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>tr</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq-\eta\|\nabla\mathcal{L}(\theta_{t})\|^{2}+\frac{\eta^{2}\ell}{2}\cdot\left(\frac{dr+d-2}{d+2}+1\right)\cdot\left(\|\nabla\mathcal{L}(\theta_{t})\|^{2}+\frac{1}{B}\mathrm{tr}(\Sigma_{MB}(\theta_{t}))\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmassumption2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_assumption">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmassumption2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Assumption 2</span></span><span id="Thmassumption2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Local Block-wise <math id="Thmassumption2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>-Effective Rank)<span id="Thmassumption2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmassumption2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmassumption2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmassumption2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The Hessian matrix <math id="Thmassumption2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(\theta_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(\theta_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> in Assumption 1 satisfies the following property:
<math id="Thmassumption2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(\theta_{t})\!=\!\mathrm{diag}(H_{1}(\theta_{t}),\ldots,H_{m}(\theta_{t}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">=</mo><mrow><mi>diag</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(\theta_{t})\!=\!\mathrm{diag}(H_{1}(\theta_{t}),\ldots,H_{m}(\theta_{t}))</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmassumption2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{i}\!:=\!\mathrm{tr}(H_{i}(\theta_{t}))/\|H_{i}(\theta_{t})\|_{\mathrm{op}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{i}\!:=\!\mathrm{tr}(H_{i}(\theta_{t}))/\|H_{i}(\theta_{t})\|_{\mathrm{op}}</annotation></semantics></math> have different upper bounds <math id="Thmassumption2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 3</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under Assumption 1 and Assumption 2 and ideal situation, assigning distinct perturbation variances across parameter blocks can yield a tighter upper bound than that of <math id="Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\mathrm{MeZO}}(\theta_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>MeZO</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\mathrm{MeZO}}(\theta_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption1" title="Assumption 1 (Local 𝑟-effective rank). ‣ Appendix D Theoretical Analysis ‣ Learning a Zeroth-Order Optimizer for Fine-Tuning LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> and Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2. ‣ Appendix D Theoretical Analysis ‣ Learning a Zeroth-Order Optimizer for Fine-Tuning LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> are directly from the theoretical analysis of MeZO <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib29" title="" class="ltx_ref">Malladi et al. (2023)</a></cite>. MeZO states the Lipschitz condition alone does not guarantee convergence in high-dimensional settings and it is necessary to <span id="A4.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">leverage the low-rank structure of the Hessian matrix</span>. Assumption 2 is consistent with the actual situation, which has been deeply researched and checked by work like Adam-mini <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib45" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang et al., 2024b</a>; <a href="#bib.bib44" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang et al., 2024a</a>)</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p4.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we consider a setting where, at each iteration, we sample a perturbation block-by-block: for the <math id="A4.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>-th parameter block, we draw noise from the distribution <math id="A4.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N(0,\sigma_{i}I_{d_{i}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N(0,\sigma_{i}I_{d_{i}})</annotation></semantics></math>, apply the perturbation to the <math id="A4.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>-th block of parameters, and perform a zeroth-order update accordingly. Let the total number of blocks be <math id="A4.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math>, and denote by <math id="A4.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}(\theta_{t,j})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}(\theta_{t,j})</annotation></semantics></math> the loss after perturbing the <math id="A4.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math>-th block at iteration <math id="A4.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>. We further denote the full loss after perturbing all <math id="A4.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math> blocks as <math id="A4.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}(\theta_{t+1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}(\theta_{t+1})</annotation></semantics></math>, and let <math id="A4.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{j}\mathcal{L}(\theta_{t,j})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{j}\mathcal{L}(\theta_{t,j})</annotation></semantics></math> denote the <math id="A4.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math>-th block of the gradient evaluated at <math id="A4.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{t,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{t,j}</annotation></semantics></math>. Here, we adopt the sphere (normalized-Gaussian) perturbation used in the original MeZO analysis for its built-in step-size control. An analogous convergence form also holds for Gaussian perturbations, as shown in prior work<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib29" title="" class="ltx_ref">Malladi et al., 2023</a>)</cite>, when the probability of large updates <math id="A4.p4.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\theta_{t+1}-\theta_{t}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\theta_{t+1}-\theta_{t}\|</annotation></semantics></math> is kept small, which ensures the required local assumptions hold with high probability.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">As shown in Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2. ‣ Appendix D Theoretical Analysis ‣ Learning a Zeroth-Order Optimizer for Fine-Tuning LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, the expected loss decrease under MeZO is bounded by</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle d_{\mathrm{MeZO}}(\theta_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>MeZO</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle d_{\mathrm{MeZO}}(\theta_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{L}(\theta_{t+1})|\theta_{t}]-\mathcal{L}(\theta_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{L}(\theta_{t+1})|\theta_{t}]-\mathcal{L}(\theta_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq-\eta\|\nabla\mathcal{L}(\theta_{t})\|^{2}+\frac{\eta^{2}\ell}{2}\cdot\left(\frac{dr+d-2}{d+2}+1\right)\cdot\left(\|\nabla\mathcal{L}(\theta_{t})\|^{2}+\frac{1}{B}\mathrm{tr}(\Sigma_{MB}(\theta_{t}))\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>B</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>tr</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq-\eta\|\nabla\mathcal{L}(\theta_{t})\|^{2}+\frac{\eta^{2}\ell}{2}\cdot\left(\frac{dr+d-2}{d+2}+1\right)\cdot\left(\|\nabla\mathcal{L}(\theta_{t})\|^{2}+\frac{1}{B}\mathrm{tr}(\Sigma_{MB}(\theta_{t}))\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Since each block-wise gradient estimate is still an unbiased estimator of the true gradient restricted to the corresponding block, we can get:</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{L}(\theta_{t,j+1})|\theta_{t,j}]-\mathcal{L}(\theta_{t,j})\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{L}(\theta_{t,j+1})|\theta_{t,j}]-\mathcal{L}(\theta_{t,j})\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-\eta\sigma_{j}^{2}\|\nabla_{j}\mathcal{L}(\theta_{t,j})\|^{2}+\frac{\eta^{2}\sigma_{j}^{4}\ell}{2}\cdot\left(\frac{dr_{j}+d-2}{d+2}+1\right)\cdot\left(\|\nabla_{j}\mathcal{L}(\theta_{t,j})\|^{2}+\frac{1}{B}\mathrm{tr}(\Sigma_{MB,j}(\theta_{t,j}))\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>j</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>j</mi><mn>4</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>B</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>tr</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\eta\sigma_{j}^{2}\|\nabla_{j}\mathcal{L}(\theta_{t,j})\|^{2}+\frac{\eta^{2}\sigma_{j}^{4}\ell}{2}\cdot\left(\frac{dr_{j}+d-2}{d+2}+1\right)\cdot\left(\|\nabla_{j}\mathcal{L}(\theta_{t,j})\|^{2}+\frac{1}{B}\mathrm{tr}(\Sigma_{MB,j}(\theta_{t,j}))\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">By summing both sides over <math id="A4.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j=1</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A4.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math> and taking expectation, we eliminate the dependence on <math id="A4.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{t,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{t,j}</annotation></semantics></math>: the right-hand side becomes a function of <math id="A4.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> only, while the left-hand side depends only on <math id="A4.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{t+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{t+1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>. This yields:</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{L}(\theta_{t+1})|\theta_{t}]-\mathcal{L}(\theta_{t})\leq-\eta\sum_{j=1}^{b}\sigma_{j}^{2}\mathbb{E}[\|\nabla_{j}\mathcal{L}(\theta_{t,j})\|^{2}|\theta_{t}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">≤</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>η</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>b</mi></munderover></mstyle><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>j</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{L}(\theta_{t+1})|\theta_{t}]-\mathcal{L}(\theta_{t})\leq-\eta\sum_{j=1}^{b}\sigma_{j}^{2}\mathbb{E}[\|\nabla_{j}\mathcal{L}(\theta_{t,j})\|^{2}|\theta_{t}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle+\sum_{j=1}^{b}\frac{\eta^{2}\sigma_{j}^{4}\ell}{2}\cdot\left(\frac{dr_{j}+d-2}{d+2}+1\right)\cdot\left(\mathbb{E}[\|\nabla_{j}\mathcal{L}(\theta_{t,j})\|^{2}|\theta_{t}]+\frac{1}{B}\mathrm{tr}(\mathbb{E}[\Sigma_{MB,j}(\theta_{t,j})|\theta_{t}])\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>b</mi></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>j</mi><mn>4</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>B</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mi>tr</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\sum_{j=1}^{b}\frac{\eta^{2}\sigma_{j}^{4}\ell}{2}\cdot\left(\frac{dr_{j}+d-2}{d+2}+1\right)\cdot\left(\mathbb{E}[\|\nabla_{j}\mathcal{L}(\theta_{t,j})\|^{2}|\theta_{t}]+\frac{1}{B}\mathrm{tr}(\mathbb{E}[\Sigma_{MB,j}(\theta_{t,j})|\theta_{t}])\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{j=1}^{b}\left[-\eta\sigma_{j}^{2}\|\nabla_{j}\mathcal{L}(\theta_{t})\|^{2}+\frac{\eta^{2}\sigma_{j}^{4}\ell}{2}\cdot\left(\frac{dr_{j}+d-2}{d+2}+1\right)\cdot\left(\|\nabla_{j}\mathcal{L}(\theta_{t})\|^{2}+\frac{1}{B}\mathrm{tr}(\Sigma_{MB}(\theta_{t}))\right)\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>b</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>j</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>j</mi><mn>4</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>B</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>tr</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{j=1}^{b}\left[-\eta\sigma_{j}^{2}\|\nabla_{j}\mathcal{L}(\theta_{t})\|^{2}+\frac{\eta^{2}\sigma_{j}^{4}\ell}{2}\cdot\left(\frac{dr_{j}+d-2}{d+2}+1\right)\cdot\left(\|\nabla_{j}\mathcal{L}(\theta_{t})\|^{2}+\frac{1}{B}\mathrm{tr}(\Sigma_{MB}(\theta_{t}))\right)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.p6.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p6.3.1" class="ltx_text">The equality in the last line follows from the condition that the Hessian matrix is block-diagonal according to Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption2" title="Assumption 2 (Local Block-wise 𝑟_𝑖-Effective Rank). ‣ Appendix D Theoretical Analysis ‣ Learning a Zeroth-Order Optimizer for Fine-Tuning LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>. Specifically, when updating block <math id="A4.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, the change in the gradient of block <math id="A4.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> (<math id="A4.p6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j_{2}\neq j_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j_{2}\neq j_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>) can be expressed as:</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{j_{2}}\mathcal{L}(\theta_{t,j_{1}})-\nabla_{j_{2}}\mathcal{L}(\theta_{t})=\int_{0}^{1}H_{j_{2}j_{1}}(\theta_{t}+sP_{j_{1}}\delta)\,\delta\,ds," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mrow><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{j_{2}}\mathcal{L}(\theta_{t,j_{1}})-\nabla_{j_{2}}\mathcal{L}(\theta_{t})=\int_{0}^{1}H_{j_{2}j_{1}}(\theta_{t}+sP_{j_{1}}\delta)\,\delta\,ds,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.p6.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p6.4.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A4.p6.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{j_{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{j_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the projection onto block <math id="A4.p6.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A4.p6.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{j_{2},j_{1}}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mrow><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{j_{2},j_{1}}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> is the <math id="A4.p6.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(j_{2},j_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(j_{2},j_{1})</annotation></semantics></math> block of the Hessian. The perturbation direction <math id="A4.p6.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math> is sampled from the standard multivariate normal distribution and scaled by the corresponding block-wise variance, i.e., <math id="A4.p6.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\sigma_{j_{1}}^{2}I_{d_{j_{1}}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\sigma_{j_{1}}^{2}I_{d_{j_{1}}})</annotation></semantics></math> for block <math id="A4.p6.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>. Under the block-diagonal assumption, <math id="A4.p6.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{j_{2},j_{1}}(\cdot)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mrow><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{j_{2},j_{1}}(\cdot)=0</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A4.p6.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j_{2}\neq j_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j_{2}\neq j_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, and thus cross-block gradient changes vanish.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Even if Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption2" title="Assumption 2 (Local Block-wise 𝑟_𝑖-Effective Rank). ‣ Appendix D Theoretical Analysis ‣ Learning a Zeroth-Order Optimizer for Fine-Tuning LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> does not hold exactly, the effect of cross-block interactions can still be controlled by bounding the operator norm of the off-diagonal blocks of the Hessian. As long as these terms remain small, the overall error introduced in the bound remains negligible.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">Note that if we set <math id="A4.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{j}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{j}=1</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A4.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math>, our upper bound reduces to the standard MeZO bound:</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{L}(\theta_{t+1})|\theta_{t}]-\mathcal{L}(\theta_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{L}(\theta_{t+1})|\theta_{t}]-\mathcal{L}(\theta_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\sum_{j=1}^{b}\left[-\eta\|\nabla_{j}\mathcal{L}(\theta_{t})\|^{2}+\frac{\eta^{2}\ell}{2}\cdot\left(\frac{dr_{j}+d-2}{d+2}+1\right)\cdot\left(\|\nabla_{j}\mathcal{L}(\theta_{t})\|^{2}+\frac{1}{B}\mathrm{tr}(\Sigma_{MB}(\theta_{t}))\right)\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>b</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>B</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>tr</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\sum_{j=1}^{b}\left[-\eta\|\nabla_{j}\mathcal{L}(\theta_{t})\|^{2}+\frac{\eta^{2}\ell}{2}\cdot\left(\frac{dr_{j}+d-2}{d+2}+1\right)\cdot\left(\|\nabla_{j}\mathcal{L}(\theta_{t})\|^{2}+\frac{1}{B}\mathrm{tr}(\Sigma_{MB}(\theta_{t}))\right)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq-\eta\|\nabla\mathcal{L}(\theta_{t})\|^{2}+\frac{\eta^{2}\ell}{2}\cdot\left(\frac{dr+d-2}{d+2}+1\right)\cdot\left(\|\nabla\mathcal{L}(\theta_{t})\|^{2}+\frac{1}{B}\mathrm{tr}(\Sigma_{MB}(\theta_{t}))\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>B</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>tr</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq-\eta\|\nabla\mathcal{L}(\theta_{t})\|^{2}+\frac{\eta^{2}\ell}{2}\cdot\left(\frac{dr+d-2}{d+2}+1\right)\cdot\left(\|\nabla\mathcal{L}(\theta_{t})\|^{2}+\frac{1}{B}\mathrm{tr}(\Sigma_{MB}(\theta_{t}))\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A4.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> is the (uniform) effective rank used in MeZO and <math id="A4.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\geq r_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\geq r_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> for any <math id="A4.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, by optimizing <math id="A4.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> for each block according to its local structure (e.g., <math id="A4.p8.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>), we can obtain a strictly tighter upper bound than <math id="A4.p8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\mathrm{MeZO}}(\theta_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>MeZO</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\mathrm{MeZO}}(\theta_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
